    "reason": "A direct function-result enum match could retain provisional Unit after its Int and USize arms failed exact terminal-type agreement. The prior recovery widened only the arm-store predicate, while result allocation, conversion, store type, and merge load still read the provisional match type. The emitter therefore omitted the result slot and emitted store void. Hoisted allocation and enum emission now derive one narrowly scoped contextual result type from the exact function-body result edge and use it consistently for allocation, numeric conversion, stores, and the merge load. Retrospective schema normalization of retained historical supervised terminal records and focused8 results; original records retained unchanged in before-schema-recovery files. No claim of current-input acceptance, whole-phase completion, current stability or performance improvement.",
